# drawtree, the tree-drawing tool of ipl_gpacks (drawtree), on tree.txt beside it, a bracket tree of 15 nodes below its root (its File menu's input data;
# the tree it builds at its start is a random draw after randomize(), the tree read from a file is not): the file named in the File menu's
# dialog, the Circle tree shown and scrolled into view, its Format menu's radius set to 30 and gap to 8 through their dialogs, q in the main
# window's strip. Without a window manager every window stands at 0 0: the tree window covers the main one but for its bottom strip.
# the File menu held open, its item Input Data; the dialog takes the file name
move 17 11
press 1
wait
move 30 30
release 1
wait
move 160 174
type tree.txt
key Return
wait
# the Circle button shows its window; the two scroll bars bring the tree into view
click 1 99 88
wait
drag 1 309 60 309 165
wait
drag 1 40 308 160 308
wait
# the tree window's Format menu, its item radius: the dialog's field stands selected and is typed over
move 22 11
press 1
wait
move 40 60
release 1
wait
move 160 160
type 30
key Return
wait
# the Format menu again, its item gap
move 22 11
press 1
wait
move 40 105
release 1
wait
move 160 160
type 8
key Return
wait
# q in the main window's strip ends the program (QuitCheck)
move 150 350
key q
